course: dictionary
lesson: 15183
title: Sealed: closed, fixed or stamped
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: «Sealed» is the past form of the verb seal, and it also works as an adjective. The clue is in the meaning: something that is sealed is closed tightly, so nothing can get in or out. «The jar was sealed, so the air could not escape.» The words could not escape tell you the jar was shut tight.
explain: «Sealed» can also mean fixed or made certain. «Our win was sealed in the last minute.» Once it is sealed, nothing can change it. A letter with a stamp or mark on it is sealed too: «The sealed envelope was on the table.» Ask which meaning fits the sentence, then swap your meaning in to check it.
explain: Some phrases use «sealed» in a special way. «My lips are sealed» does not mean your mouth is shut. It means you will keep a secret. When a word has more than one meaning, the sentence around it tells you which one to use.
fact: Sealed means closed tightly so that nothing can get in or out.
fact: «Sealed» can also mean fixed or made certain, as in «Our win was sealed».
fact: A sealed letter or envelope has a seal or stamp on it, and it may hide a secret.
fact: «My lips are sealed» means I will keep the secret.
fact: In safety, food and medicine should come in a sealed package; if the seal is broken, do not use it.
exercise: «The lid was sealed so the cookies stayed fresh.» What does sealed mean here? | Opened wide for everyone | Painted in bright colours | Lost under the table | *Closed tightly so nothing can get in or out
exercise: Maya says, «My lips are sealed.» What does she mean? | She is sealing an envelope | She has a cold and cannot speak | She is very hungry | *She will keep the secret
exercise: Which verb does «sealed» come from? | *seal | steal | sail
test: «The deal was sealed when both sides shook hands.» Which meaning of sealed fits best? | *Fixed and certain, so it could not change | Closed tightly so nothing gets in | Painted with bright colours
test: A sealed package of medicine has a broken seal. What should you do? | Use it quickly before it spoils | *Do not use it | Put the seal back on and keep using it
exam: Which sentence uses «sealed» to mean closed tightly so nothing can get in? | *The jar was sealed, so the air stayed inside | Our team's win was sealed in the last minute | My lips are sealed, so I cannot tell you
